+/* The launch counter of the copy kernels that vkCmdCopyMemoryIndirectKHR
+ * records on a queue without a copy engine, as the proprietary driver
+ * counts its kernel launches (libnvidia-eglcore.so 615.78.08): word 2 of a
+ * 0x100-byte scratch block of GPU-only device memory (ELF 0xc5b52a /
+ * ELF 0xc5a490), reset at the command buffer's first launch with a host
+ * semaphore release of 0 and an acquire of 0 (ELF 0xc5b300), increased by
+ * the RELEASE0 of each launch's QMD (ELF 0xaee500).  A barrier after such
+ * launches waits for the counter to reach the number of launches (host
+ * ACQ_CIRC_GEQ) and issues a compute NO_OPERATION, without idling the
+ * compute engine (ELF 0xc5a530), then invalidates the destination's caches;
+ * the end of the command buffer waits for the counter
+ * once more (ELF 0xc5c980 -> ELF 0xc5c500 -> ELF 0xc5a530).  A secondary
+ * command buffer has a counter of its own; the primary that executes it
+ * does not count its launches.  Volta/Turing count every dispatch on
+ * cmd->sked's counter, which this reuses there.
